# Four-step problem-solving framework

Source documenting a generic productivity skill framed as a four-step workflow improvement cycle: Audit, Apply, Iterate, Scale. The framework involves systematically auditing current workflows, applying optimization methods, iterating based on measured results, and scaling effective practices. Confidence: 0.7. Priority: low. Single-source skill with limited depth.
